I tried to refute the NARROWED grade in both directions and could not.

**What I read myself.** The Letter in full, v3 (alphaXiv fullText), and the companion gr-qc/9802046v2, pp.1, 4, 12-22, 24-25, 27, 29. Every quotation the audit attributes to them is at source as stated:
- results (1)-(4);
- eqs.(3), (5), (8), (9)-(13);
- the punctured-interval parentheticals;
- footnote [14] on averaged flare-out;
- [11] def. 4.1.3 and eq.(36);
- [11] eq.(33), which keeps theta^2 and drops it only by using theta=0 on the throat;
- [11] eq.(53) and the p.20 warning that this "has nothing to do with ... ANEC";
- [11] eqs.(75)-(77).

The driven.py:96-98 ellipsis does remove "and reaching the other universe then one must have passed a throat as defined above and", which leaves "this throat" with nothing to refer to.

**Tree sites.** I read foliation.py:244-248 and driven.py:94-98, 311-312, 493-499, 517-518 and 893-896. The drift items (a) to (d) are accurate:
- (a) foliation.py fuses results (3) and (4).
- (b) driven.py:895 writes "averaged NEC" without "transverse".
- (c) the elision above.
- (d) the "corridor" at driven.py:261-268 holds its areal radius to +/-1%. That is not an area minimum, and nothing in the file shows a theta_pm = 0 sphere with null flare-out. driven.py's own REFUSED line gives the impossibility claim to Olum alone.

**Computation.** I ran the auditor's script: exit 0, ALL PASS, 16 checks. C1 agrees with [11] eq.(90), the throat is flared iff T_vv <= 0.

**Why not STANDS.** The drift is real and READ at source, not inferred from a restatement. foliation.py's line also states a pointwise-on-an-interval claim the Letter does not make.

**Why not WRONG.** No counterexample to results (1)-(4) under the published hypotheses exists. C2 and C3 are UNSAT, and the vacuity guards are SAT. The Letter's discrepancies (theta^2 dropped, C4; the punctured interval, C5) are correctly recorded as discrepancies only. C4c confirms the toy breaks eq.(3).

**Two corrections that do not move the grade.**

(i) The "ADDED: traversability" drift item is overstated. The Letter itself states result (1) as "A time-dependent traversable wormhole will have two throats", so listing traversability is faithful to the Letter's own wording. The correct form of the point is that the proof assumes a throat and the traversal-to-throat link is asserted. That point is already H8.

(ii) H5 equates the Letter's result (4) with [11] eq.(53), but eq.(53) is ON the throat (u=0). Result (4) is about surfaces pushed out along the congruence, over an open interval, and that is the form driven.py:94-95 cites. I machine-checked a pointwise lemma: off the throat, -8piT = theta' + theta^2/2 + sigma^2 with sigma^2 >= 0 gives sgn(T) <= -sgn(theta'). The z3 negation is UNSAT and the guard is SAT. So the pushed-out (4) follows whenever averaged flare-out persists on Sigma(u) for u in an interval. Dominated convergence gives that persistence if {theta'=0} on Sigma has measure zero. Without that extra hypothesis, which neither document states, (4) as the tree uses it is OPEN rather than proven. The audit's what_would_change_the_grade already anticipates this ("OPEN for (4) if the tree rests on the pushed-out form"), and driven.py:94-95 does rest on it. This narrows result (4) further; it does not overturn NARROWED for the entry as a whole, since results (1)-(3) stand.

**No datum enters.** Only sign(G) is used.
